    "result_text": "Only draft claims can be edited now, and a voided claim keeps its number. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 acceptance tests.\n\n**Server**\n- **Editing a non-draft is refused:** new step `CheckClaimEditDraft.java`, added to the claim edit endpoint (`claims/{claimId}.PUT.yml`) right after the claim is loaded. For any claim that isn't a DRAFT it sends back a 409 saying to void the claim and add a new one. The refusal happens before anything is saved or audited, so nothing is written to the store or the audit file.\n- **Voiding keeps the number:** `ApplyClaimAction.java` no longer clears the number on void, so `CLAIM_VOIDED` carries it (`... number=1`). Numbers still come from the sheet's counter, which only goes up, so a voided number is never reused.\n\n**Front end** (`Claims.tsx`)\n- Clicking **Edit** on a claim that isn't a draft shows the error on the claim row (`claim-error`) and doesn't open the editor. Clicking Edit or any status button again clears it.\n- If the claim gets opened by someone else while your editor is open, saving now shows the server's 409 message in `claim-form-error` instead of a generic one.\n\nClaims that were voided before this change still have no number, because the old code deleted it and there's no way to get it back.",
